From 6d8b0a5d87a9cd97c11c5f09f2061e88a8c078e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvia420-bit <salvia420@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:52:42 -0330
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Vehicles (holtburger fork): 1070 fixes + M3 world-loop
 residual

Found on the first real-GPU look at the Hellcat demo (2026-11-01):
- Seat in the stand-in balloon's basket (0, 0, 5.75): Setup 0x020016F1 draws its
  balloon from 19 m up, so at the 0.3 scale the old (0, -0.5, 0.6) seated the
  pilot ~5 m below the basket, for retail observers too. Gun muzzle moved to
  the basket (0, 0.8, 6.0).

M3 residual (whole world loop while vehicles exist):
- Diagnostics: bring-up items over 30 ms split by cause ([HEAVYADD]: GC pause,
  indoor cells, link weenie fetch / construct / SetLinkProperties, physics init /
  placement / notify, who loaded the landblock), landblock loads outside the
  vehicle loader by origin ([LOAD]), per-landblock single-threaded work and its
  worst heartbeat ([LBSINGLE]), lazy indoor-cell builds outside items ([CELLS]).
- Landblocks loaded by a vehicle-only landblock's physics step, heartbeat or
  object relocation are vehicle-only too (they were ordinary: no budget, no
  spawn warm-up, cold generator camps).
- Link children's weenies (a house's hooks / slumlord / storage) fetched on
  CreateWorldObjects' background task (vehicle_landblock_budget): a cottage's
  53 links 62 ms -> ~1 ms on the landblock tick.
- The spawn warm-up builds each weenie's Setup parts into the permanent
  GfxObjCache off-thread (first InitPhysicsObj of a model: 45-106 ms).
- Stall classification tests GC before the vehicle phase.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
